there are tons of easy ways you can pass  the time but why not fill your time with  some experiments while you are just  sitting around would you believe that  you can actually walk on raw eggs  without them breaking stay tuned to see  how if you are new to our channel click  the red subscribe button to see more  videos like this today we are showing  you ten fun and unusual experiments to  waste your time on plastic milk what  would you say if we told you you could  turn milk into plastic well you can and  it's very easy all you need is one cup  of hot milk one coffee mug with four  teaspoons of vinegar paper towels and a  spoon combine the hot milk and vinegar  in the coffee mug and stir you will  notice the milk starting to curdle after  the make sure he's cooled spoon the  curds out and place them onto the paper  towels to dry press out all the water  and then remove the paper towels now you  have case in plastic which you can mold  into any shape of your choosing make  objects disappear though it may seem  like a magic trick this experiment works  by playing with light you will need a  beaker vegetable oil and one or more  glass objects fill the beaker with  vegetable oil and place the various  glass objects inside you will notice  that the objects become hard to see to  take it a step further find a glass  container you can pour vegetable oil  into and drop it into the beaker did it  completely disappear glitter slime a  great way to kick your DIY slime up a  notch is to add glitter the easiest way  to make glitter slime is to get one  bottle of Elmer's glitter glue one cup  of water 1 teaspoon of borax and an  extra tablespoon of water first mix 1  teaspoon of borax with one cup of water  next empty the bottle of Elmer's glitter  glue into a separate bowl and add the  extra tablespoon of water then combine  the borax mixture to the glue mixture  and blend together with your hands the  mixture will quickly turn into your  pretty glittery slime unbreakable egg  this experiment will allow you to bounce  a raw egg without it breaking all you  need is a glass white vinegar and a raw  egg first place the raw egg into the  glass without breaking it then pour the  vinegar into the glass until the egg is  completely submerged over the next 24  hours you will notice  eggs will start to lose its shell once  it looks completely gone dry off the egg  and try to bounce it from a couple of  inches off the table fish for ice on a  boring day were too hot to fish for  actual fish try fishing for ice for this  easy activity you will need a glass of  water a few ice cubes table salt and a  piece of string drop the ice into the  glass of water and close the string on  top  pull the string out and notice how you  probably haven't caught anything place  the string back in the water but this  time sprinkle some salt on top wait a  few minutes then pull your string back  up and admire your catches magnetic  slime there are several DIY slime  tutorials online and magnetic slime is  one of the coolest to make your own you  will need liquid starch Elmer's glue  iron oxide powder disposable bowls and a  neo diem magnet for 1/2 cup of liquid  starch into a bowl add 2 tablespoons of  iron oxide powder and then stir next add  a quarter cup of glue and stir until  well mixed the slime will start to form  you can take it out and start mixing  with your hands which may get dirty get  rid of excess water with a paper towel  and start playing with your magnetic  slime and neodym magnets ivory soap  monster this experiment lets you make a  crazy ivory soap monster as well as your  own soap at the same time all you need  is a dish of water a microwave and a bar  of ivory so place the bar of soap in the  dish of water and microwave on HIGH for  2 minutes now watch as the soap starts  to transform into a fluffy monster wait  for the fluff to cool and then you can  play with the mixture or make your own  soap balls just add your own ingredients  like oatmeal or lavender and let the  mixture dry overnight  fluffy slime if you have a need for even  more fluff try the fluffy slime  experiment for this project you need a  large bowl 5 bottles of Elmer's glue  shaving cream baking soda contact  solution food coloring foaming hand soap  and googan pour the 5 bottles of glue  into a large bowl then add two and a  half tablespoons of baking soda and mix  next add one and a quarter cups of  shaving cream to the mixture and keep  stirring add your food coloring and a  couple pumps of hand soap and keep  stirring finally add drops of contact  solution to the mix until you can play  with the slime without it sticking to  your hands  popsicle stick harmonica have you ever  wanted to try the harmonica but didn't  have the cash to do so try this easy to  make popsicle stick harmonica instead  for this you need two wide popsicle  sticks two rubber bands one strip of  paper that is the size of the popsicle  sticks and two toothpicks first place  the piece of paper between the popsicle  sticks and fasten each end with a rubber  band  then slide a piece of the toothpick  between the popsicle sticks on top of  the paper and on the inside of the  rubber band finally do the same on the  other side but under the piece of paper  now make some awesome music with your  new instruments walking on eggs you may  have never thought about literally  walking on eggshells but it's a fun way  to frighten a boring day gather 6-8  cartons of eggs a trash bag and  disinfectant wipes first make sure there  are no broken eggs if you are indoors  lay a garbage bag down in case things  get messy  next place the full egg cartons into two  rows making sure all the pointed ends  are facing down with a friends help  stand on the eggs with your bare feet  finally take a few steps while keeping  your weight evenly distributed did any  of the eggs break which one of these  experiments are you excited to waste  your time on let us know in the comment  section below and for more fun  activities check out our 10 awesome  science experiments you can do right now  at home  [Music]  [Music]
 

